      "description": "<p>The 8ft statue, installed in Phoenix last week to mark one year since Kirk’s killing, was found painted red</p><p>A newly unveiled statue of the rightwing activist Charlie Kirk was vandalized at the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2026/sep/09/turning-point-usa-charlie-kirk-killing-one-year-later\">Turning Point USA</a> headquarters in Phoenix, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona\">Arizona</a>.</p><p>The statue was found with red spray-paint. A nearby poster memorial in front of the statue was vandalized with red paint as well.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/13/charlie-kirk-statue-vandalized-tpusa-arizona\">Continue reading...</a>",
